5.2 ODR-MMBTOOLS (OpenDigitalRadio)

DABcast is a management interface designed to control external tools from the
ODR-mmbTools project (https://www.opendigitalradio.org/). These tools include:

  - ODR-DabMux     (DAB multiplexer)
  - ODR-AudioEnc   (audio encoder)
  - ODR-PadEnc     (PAD encoder)
  - ODR-DabMod     (modulator)

These tools are NOT included in the DABcast source code or binary. They are
installed separately (via an install script or manually) and are invoked as
independent system processes. DABcast communicates with them through standard
interfaces (ZMQ, EDI, FIFO, command-line arguments).

The ODR-mmbTools components are licensed under the GNU General Public License
(GPL v2 or v3, depending on the component) by the OpenDigitalRadio association.
The restrictions of this DABcast license do not apply to ODR-mmbTools, and this
license does not modify, limit, or override the rights granted by the GPL to
users of those tools.

